{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1093964-real-world-time-moons-weather-in-cofd-games","id":1093964,"title":"Real world Time, Moons & Weather in CofD games","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-17T20:24:18-07:00","id":1093964,"title":"Real world Time, Moons & Weather in CofD games","content":"<b>Are you using real world calendar, astrological or weather data?</b> CoD universe is based on our real world, but it also is different in subtle manners.<br /> <br /> As I run <b>Werewolf </b>games, I use Moon calendars or astrological charts to look for Luna Phases or some interesting plot ideas in there. I check my sources and use local weather if there was intriguing or non-ordinary Weather phenomenon.<br /> <br /> To expend topic, let\u2019s share our sources and maybe apps to track this kind of things. I can strongly recommend <i>Weather\u2019s Undergournd</i> <b><a href=\"https://www.wunderground.com/history/airport/2017/05/17/DailyHistory.html?MR=1\" target=\"_blank\">Historical Weather search engine</a></b> \u2013 you simply enter location and date in past \u2013 and you get exact weather and Moon on that date. Limit is only to year 1945, but for near-modern usage \u2013 it\u2019s golden!<br /> <br /> <b>If someone have similar app or site for finding at least Moons up to year 800 A.D. or even earlier \u2013 I would much more be grateful for link.</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-18-2017, 03:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T21:37:47-07:00","id":1093984,"title":"","content":"When I used to LARP we would generally just use the actual date, time, weather, and astronomical events.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T03:34:38-07:00","id":1094058,"title":"","content":"Found Moon Phases table from 2000 BCE to 4000 CE - <a href=\"http://astropixels.com/ephemeris/phasescat/phasescat.html\" target=\"_blank\">Here it is</a> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Notice: Those dates don't miss 'year zero', so -199 here is our 200 BCE.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-18-2017, 01:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T10:05:55-07:00","id":1094196,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://thornews.com/2015/09/27/the-viking-calendar/\" target=\"_blank\">How to translate Viking to Gregorian Calendar</a> dates!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T10:26:57-07:00","id":1094212,"title":"","content":"I remember being surprised when I looked into this and realized that half of the time, moonrise happens during the day. Not such a huge deal in standard W:tF, but it kinda throws a wrench into things if you're writing something where everybody cares if the moon is up and not just the people who have moon based kuruth triggers.<br /> <br /> I eventually decided that the moon had to be up AND the sun had to be down for things to get hairy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9001,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","user":"solidork","date":". 05-18-2017, 01:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T10:36:38-07:00","id":1094216,"title":"","content":"Might make for a specific caste among the Temple of Apollo, the 'Sunborn' or something. Maybe even the Pure might approve, if they associate Helios with dimming Luna's power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-17T11:28:26-07:00","id":1104797,"title":"","content":"Found site to <a href=\"https://www.timeanddate.com/calendar/custom.html?year=799&amp;country=21\" target=\"_blank\">create days of week calendar based on year you choose</a> - in example year 799 for Sweden I run with now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-17T21:14:13-07:00","id":1104971,"title":"","content":"Using this <a href=\"https://thornews.com/2015/09/27/the-viking-calendar/\" target=\"_blank\">article on change of Gregorian Calendar to the Norse</a><a href=\"https://thornews.com/2015/09/27/the-viking-calendar/\" target=\"_blank\"> one</a> ( with added translation of days of week ), I have this opening paragraph for the game:<br /> <br /> <i>In M\u00e1nadagr,</i><i> thirteenth day of Month Goa in the year of the Lord 799 in Temple at Uppsala is starting </i><i>D\u00edsabl\u00f3t \u2013 greatest festival of those time, on which are made prays to Thor, Odin and Frejr for blessing in the coming summer and people are asking d\u00edsir for help in their life. There are also made alliances and prepared plans for Vikings \u2013 raids \u2013 in this year.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-28-2017, 06:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-18T19:38:06-07:00","id":1105258,"title":"","content":"I've used Weather Underground frequently. For moon, sunrise, twilight, etc, I currently use <a href=\"http://www.sunrisesunset.com/predefined.asp\" target=\"_blank\">this site</a>. I can print out a month with a good deal of data for each day. I'm running vampire games, but werewolves factor in. Plus, several kindred events are structured around moon phases, so I make sure the phase is on the calendar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-10T20:53:12-08:00","id":1166594,"title":"","content":"I try to use constant penalties for senses related actions at night for <i><b>everyone</b></i>, based on Moon Phase. It's why I check those Moon Phase tables in the first place - mainly for Werewolf. It works like this for <u>anyone</u> in CoD game:<ul><li>On New Moon is -2 penalty</li> <li>At Full Moon it's no penalty ( as it's 'almost bright as in day' )</li> <li>At any other Moon Phase it's -1 penalty</li> </ul>Simple and elegant. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It's also nicely highlight that 'Irraka are secretive and always up to something' and 'Rahu wants simple and straight forward answers, like in day'. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And I want to point that Uratha have all bonus to senses related actions in any form, even in human Hishu they have +1 bonus. So werewolves still have slight edge in night over any other enemy. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T10:27:47-07:00","id":1221752,"title":"","content":"Found great page for marking of time relation to the geopolitical situation - <b><a href=\"https://www.timemaps.com/history/\" target=\"_blank\">Timemaps Archive</a></b>. Just point nearest date on the list and you can see how looked whole world in that time. Great visualization of context for historical games! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}